1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,488
Half-twist a paper loop and cut it down the middle.

2
00:00:04,788 --> 00:00:05,971
Two rings?

3
00:00:05,971 --> 00:00:06,562
Nope.

4
00:00:07,062 --> 00:00:09,765
It falls open into one long ring.

5
00:00:10,265 --> 00:00:11,340
Follow one half.

6
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:13,826
The twist joins it to the other half.

7
00:00:14,126 --> 00:00:17,253
So both halves are one strip, twice as long.

8
00:00:17,753 --> 00:00:21,290
Cut a third from the edge instead: two rings, linked.

9
00:00:21,790 --> 00:00:22,538
Two?
